// An explicit annotation normally wins. A fn ALIAS does not lose to one: `let p: fn(i32) -> i32 = f` records
// the fn-pointer TYPE text, which says nothing about WHICH fn, so the alias -- the only thing that lets `p(x)`
// reach `f` -- would be discarded and the call would crash. Measured: unannotated worked, annotated crashed,
