        // difference is that the second spells `f` inside a macro. Scanning the token list closes it. The same
        // blindness bit CHK-2b, which had to look for moved names in macro tokens for the same reason.
        // CT-146: a macro's arguments are raw TOKENS, so this walk saw fn NAMES but never a closure LITERAL:
        // `println!("{}", ap(|x| x + 1, 7))` emitted NO __closure_ fn and the cell pointed at a symbol that
        // does not exist. Reparse each comma segment -- the same s9_vec_seg_src/s9_reparse_expr pair vec! and
        // format! already use -- and recurse, so a closure inside a macro arg is lifted like any other.
