// by dropped-bodies.py at 350 bodies across 89 files that score clean, headed by rustc_session/src/options.rs
// (72 parsed, 2 emitted). Two recursive passes mirror the top-level ones and run at the same points, so the
// global order (all lifts, then all fns) is preserved.
// A module fn is emitted under its QUALIFIED name, which is what an outside caller emits (`call parse::foo`),
// and ALSO under its bare ident when nothing already holds that name -- an inside-the-module call is bare. The
// bare emission is guarded because two definitions of one name collide under ld's dedup-by-name, which is the
// same constraint the trait-default pass records.
